New retained evidence is below. I did not score.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Федеральный закон от 24 июля 2023 года № 329-ФЗ Об исполнении федерального бюджета за 2022 год","publisher":"Российская газета","publication_date":"2023-07-25","url":"https://rg.ru/documents/2023/07/25/fz329-site-dok.html","claim":"Putin signed the law approving the 2022 federal budget execution report; it records 27.824 trillion rubles in revenue, 31.119 trillion rubles in spending, and a 3.295 trillion ruble deficit.","locator":"Article 1, lines 66-79","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary publication of the enacted federal law with exact budget totals and signature date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly covers 2022 execution","ruler_attribution":"direct presidential approval of the budget execution law, though execution was carried by the wider fiscal apparatus","contrary_evidence":["The result was a deficit, not the budget balance implied by the original 2022 plan."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Росстат представляет данные о естественном движении населения в декабре 2022 года","publisher":"Росстат","publication_date":"2023-02-10","url":"https://rosstat.gov.ru/folder/313/document/197667","claim":"Rosstat reported that in 2022 Russia recorded 1,306,162 births, 1,905,778 deaths, and a natural decrease of 599,616 people, with deaths down 22.1 percent from 2021.","locator":"press release text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official statistics release with precise annual demographic totals.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly covers 2022","ruler_attribution":"indirect to Putin; the figures are official outcomes of the state statistical system and wartime context rather than a personal decree","contrary_evidence":["The release also shows continued population decline despite the improvement versus 2021."],"lenses":["6B.6","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Росстат представляет информацию о границе бедности в IV квартале 2022 года","publisher":"Росстат","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://rosstat.gov.ru/folder/313/document/200416","claim":"Rosstat said 2022 poverty was 10.5 percent, or 15.3 million people, and attributed the decline to higher social payments and targeted social programs along with wage and pension growth.","locator":"press release text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statistics page with specific poverty and policy-cause language, but the exact publication date was not visible in the accessible snippet.","final_evidence_use":"discovery_only","period_fit":"directly covers 2022","ruler_attribution":"mixed; the outcome reflects Putin-era social policy, but also inflation and broader income dynamics","contrary_evidence":["The same page shows poverty remained large in absolute terms, so this is an improvement rather than a solved problem."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.8","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Правительство проиндексировало пенсии, прожиточный минимум и минимальный размер оплаты труда на 10%","publisher":"Правительство России","publication_date":"2022-05-30","url":"https://government.ru/docs/45559/","claim":"The government indexed pensions, the subsistence minimum, and the minimum wage by 10 percent from 1 June 2022, explicitly saying the decision was taken on Putin's order.","locator":"document summary and decree text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government decree with a clear policy change and attribution, though the page itself timed out on direct open.","final_evidence_use":"discovery_only","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"directly attributable to Putin's order and the government's implementation","contrary_evidence":["This is compensatory crisis policy, not proof of a durable welfare improvement on its own."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.7","6B.8","8B.2","8B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Instructions following a meeting on socioeconomic support for regions","publisher":"President of Russia","publication_date":"2022-04-10","url":"https://en.kremlin.ru/acts/assignments/orders/copy/68175","claim":"Putin instructed the government to assess families whose members lost jobs, expand access to social support for families with children, provide additional unemployment support, index pensions and benefits, raise wages and the minimum wage, and allocate extra federal funds for regional infrastructure and domestic-demand support.","locator":"instruction text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential instructions with specific policy tasks; the page timed out on direct open but the search snippet was detailed and attributable.","final_evidence_use":"discovery_only","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"direct presidential instruction to the government and regions","contrary_evidence":["The instructions show response to shock and hardship, not an unambiguous preplanned welfare expansion."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.6","8B.2","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Отчет о ходе реализации государственной программы Российской Федерации Развитие здравоохранения за 2022 год","publisher":"Министерство здравоохранения Российской Федерации","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://static-0.minzdrav.gov.ru/system/attachments/attaches/000/066/015/original/%D0%A3%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%82_%D0%B7%D0%B0_2022_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D0%B4.pdf?1712214393=","claim":"The 2022 health-program report shows no critical deviations at the top level and lists the cash-execution reporting structure for the national health program, including unexecuted appropriations of 55,538,493.56.","locator":"page 0 summary table","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary ministry PDF opened directly; the claim comes from the report's first-page summary table.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly covers 2022 implementation","ruler_attribution":"indirect to Putin; this is ministry implementation inside a Putin-era program framework rather than a personal act","contrary_evidence":["The report is self-reporting and does not by itself prove real-world health gains."],"lenses":["6B.4","6B.5","6B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Валерий Фальков: в этом году было выделено самое большое количество бюджетных мест за последние 10-15 лет","publisher":"Министерство науки и высшего образования Российской Федерации","publication_date":"2022-11-22","url":"https://www.minobrnauki.gov.ru/press-center/news/novosti-ministerstva/61294/","claim":"The ministry said 588,000 budget-funded university places were allocated in 2022, the largest number in 10-15 years, plus 30,000 extra master's places for priority programs because of the difficult geopolitical situation.","locator":"news article text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official ministry press release with a concrete allocation figure, but the page returned a 502 on direct open and is retained from the search snippet.","final_evidence_use":"discovery_only","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"indirect but substantial; this reflects Putin-era education policy priorities implemented through the ministry","contrary_evidence":["The release proves input and allocation, not that quality or labor-market outcomes improved equally."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.5","8B.2","8B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Instructions on developing unmanned aircraft systems","publisher":"President of Russia","publication_date":"2022-12-30","url":"https://en.kremlin.ru/acts/assignments/orders/copy/70312","claim":"Putin ordered the government to create a commission on unmanned aircraft systems chaired by First Deputy Prime Minister Andrei Belousov and to draft a 2030 and 2035 strategy, procurement plan, certification framework, training system, and related interagency measures.","locator":"instruction text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary Kremlin instructions with named chair, deadlines, and implementation tasks, directly visible in the search result snippet.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"directly attributable to Putin's command authority over the cabinet and security ministries","contrary_evidence":["This is strong evidence of mobilization and planning, but not yet proof of durable delivery by year-end."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}

Gap status:
1B direct nuclear doctrine and appointments - partly resolved; the existing file set still leans on rhetoric and governance context rather than a clean 2022 primary doctrine package.
5B budget execution - resolved by the federal budget execution law and the official macro record.
5B distributional evidence - partly resolved; poverty, pensions, and wage support are clearer, but region-by-region beneficiary detail is still thin.
5B economic team and delegated authority beyond Nabiullina - partly resolved; the new Belousov and cabinet instructions help, but the broader decision chain is still incomplete.
6B direct 2022 health, education, welfare delivery, and budget execution - resolved in part; health-program reporting, education allocations, and social-support decrees now give direct implementation evidence.
6B subnational and distributional evidence - partly resolved; the national picture is clearer, but regional and group-level breakdowns remain incomplete.
6B excess mortality, life expectancy, and vaccination catch-up - partly resolved; demographic and health-program records improve this, but vaccination catch-up is still not directly closed here.
7B direct 2022 personal assets, beneficial ownership, or family-linked concealment - not recoverable in this round; public disclosures and direct 2022 ownership proof remain thin.
7B direct correction of false claims versus doubling down - partly resolved in the existing dossier, but this round did not recover a cleaner primary correction record.
7B appointment favoritism versus competence - partly resolved; network/patronage patterns remain stronger than direct 2022 appointment evidence.
8B day-to-day operational control and personnel shifts - partly resolved; the new interagency commission and repeated economic meetings show control, but not full command-chain detail.
8B industrial-policy and budget-execution evidence - resolved; the 2022 budget law, health-program report, regional support instructions, and UAV instructions give direct implementation records.
8B technocratic management versus Putin's own control - partly resolved; stabilization is clearer, but attribution still splits between Putin's directives and delegated technocrats.

Blockers and failed directions:
- `rosstat.gov.ru`, `government.ru`, `minobrnauki.gov.ru`, and some `kremlin.ru` pages timed out or returned 502 on direct open, so a few items were retained from official search snippets rather than fully opened pages.
- No credible 2022 primary source for Putin's own private asset disclosure was recovered; the public Kremlin archive exposed only earlier-year disclosure pages, so that gap remains not recoverable from this round.
